                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9784af92-aed0-37ff-8919-275ed25a05c9",
                        "entry_id": "148e0179-c074-3331-9538-c573d57534f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "diminutive of пятно́ (pjatnó): (small) speck, spot, blot, blemish, stain"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "diminutive",
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd1ab65d-c0d4-407e-901b-c8e9a1e4d2f5",
                                "sense_id": "9784af92-aed0-37ff-8919-275ed25a05c9",
                                "text": "А ведьма, между тем, поднялась так высоко, что одним только черным пятнышком мелькала вверху. Но где ни показывалось пятнышко, там звезды, одна за другою, пропадали на небе.",
                                "translation": "And the witch by this time had risen so high that she only looked like a little dark spot up above; but wherever that spot went, one star after another disappeared from heaven.",
                                "english": "And the witch by this time had risen so high that she only looked like a little dark spot up above; but wherever that spot went, one star after another disappeared from heaven."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
